  "brief": "AppLovin is reportedly in talks to acquire Criteo, a Paris-based ad tech firm, in a deal that could target expansion in the retail media landscape.\n\nAppLovin / Criteo (Rumored): AppLovin and Criteo Deal Rumors. AppLovin is reportedly in talks to acquire Criteo, a Paris-based ad tech firm [4, 5, 6]. The deal is still in the early stages, with no official announcement made yet [1, 2, 3]. The acquisition would potentially target expansion in the retail media landscape [4, 6]. No further details have been disclosed about the potential deal [1, 2, 3].\nTPG / Bill Holdings (Completed): TPG and Bill Holdings Deal. TPG and Bill Holdings have completed their deal [14]. Bill Holdings shares surged on reports of the looming deal [13]. The deal was expected to happen within days [11, 12, 15].\nBASF / Evonik (Rumored): BASF and Evonik Takeover Rumors. BASF is considering further concessions in its bid for Evonik [17, 19]. Evonik has rejected BASF's $12.5B takeover bid, but leaves room for 'purely informational' talks [20]. BASF has increased its bid for Evonik to over €11 billion [23]. A higher BASF bid alone will not win support for Evonik takeover [16].\nBeeline Holdings, Inc. / TYTL (Announced): Beeline Holdings to Acquire TYTL. Beeline Holdings, Inc. is acquiring TYTL in an all-stock deal [24, 25]. The deal aims to expand into tokenized home equity and blockchain-based real estate finance [24, 25]. No further information is available on the current stage of the deal [24, 25].\nWynnchurch Capital / Luxfer Holdings (Completed): Wynnchurch Capital Acquires Luxfer Holdings. Wynnchurch Capital has acquired Luxfer Holdings in a take-private deal [26, 27, 28]. The acquisition was completed at $17.37 per share [26, 27]. Luxfer shareholders approved the deal in early November [28].\nAdvent / Boardroom (Rumored): Advent to Buy Boardroom. Advent is in talks to buy Boardroom on strong Asia services demand [29, 30]. The deal is rumored at this point [29, 30].\nDaiichi Life / Challenger (Announced): Daiichi Life and Challenger. Daiichi Life made a takeover bid for Challenger [34]. Challenger rejected the takeover bid [32, 33, 34]. The deal was announced [31].\nTransom Capital / SoundThinking (Completed): Transom Capital Acquires SoundThinking. Transom Capital has acquired SoundThinking, a public safety technology company [35, 36, 37]. The deal is now completed [35, 36, 37].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- DoorDash Stock Falls as Instacart Deal Scrutiny and Competitive Pressure Weigh on Shares [38].\n- Sanofi Weighs Takeover of US Drugmaker Insmed [39].\n- Korea's $14.9B Naver-Dunamu crypto deal nears final antitrust verdict [40].",
